1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,764
This is Patchwork, an editorial workbench for a small,
fictional museum.

2
00:00:04,814 --> 00:00:07,951
Every story exists in English, Finnish and Spanish,

3
00:00:07,981 --> 00:00:12,328
and it lives in a real Sanity project, whose ID you can see on
screen.

4
00:00:13,080 --> 00:00:16,427
The loom story is not ready. Four gates block it:

5
00:00:16,477 --> 00:00:22,457
no image description, no summary, no access note, and a link
that only says click here.

6
00:00:23,210 --> 00:00:26,396
I load an authored suggestion. It is fixture copy;

7
00:00:26,446 --> 00:00:30,240
no AI runs in the app. Saving sends one Sanity transaction,

8
00:00:30,270 --> 00:00:37,789
guarded by the revision ID of every document it read, and the
server reads the receipt back before it shows success.

9
00:00:38,530 --> 00:00:42,454
Because English changed, Finnish and Spanish are now marked
stale.

10
00:00:42,504 --> 00:00:46,307
Each translation remembers the English revision it was based
on.

11
00:00:46,357 --> 00:00:50,461
These still match, so I confirm each one against English
version two.

12
00:00:53,540 --> 00:00:59,548
Next, a demo reviewer role, clearly labelled and not real
authentication, approves each language.

13
00:00:59,598 --> 00:01:04,357
Every approval stores a fingerprint of the exact content and
source versions.

14
00:01:07,610 --> 00:01:11,847
With three fresh approvals, the publisher writes a separate
public edition.

15
00:01:11,897 --> 00:01:16,476
Drafts live under the drafts path; the edition is an ordinary
published document.

16
00:01:17,230 --> 00:01:20,773
The visitor page reads only Sanity's published perspective.

17
00:01:20,823 --> 00:01:23,635
Here is the loom story, in all three languages.

18
00:01:25,480 --> 00:01:30,852
Anyone can check this without a token. This is the public
dataset's query URL,

19
00:01:30,882 --> 00:01:34,207
returning the same edition and its operation ID.

20
00:01:34,960 --> 00:01:38,017
Back in the workbench, I correct the access evidence.

21
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:40,326
Every affected approval clears at once,

22
00:01:40,356 --> 00:01:45,638
and the public edition stays exactly as it was, until someone
reviews and publishes again.

23
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:52,492
The history keeps each change with its reason, its actor, and
a full before and after snapshot.

24
00:01:52,542 --> 00:01:55,844
Restoring creates a new draft. It never republishes.

25
00:01:56,590 --> 00:02:03,773
The museum and its content are synthetic, and these checks are
editorial prompts, not accessibility certification.

26
00:02:03,823 --> 00:02:07,453
The code, tests and live verification notes are on GitHub.
